<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # The Talents Around Us – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Talents Around Us</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Who Will Perform in the Fiestas Patrias Activities?</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: productive: Compose simple descriptive texts. interactive: Edit short texts with peers.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write short descriptive paragraphs about preparing for Fiestas Patrias celebrations (e.g., 'If I practice the traditional dance every day, I will perform well in the parade.' 'I will wear my pollera during the school celebration.'). Can write coherent, simple descriptive texts about Fiestas Patrias events (e.g., 'First, the honor roll student will carry the Panamanian flag, then the school band will play, and finally, the dancers will perform traditional dances.'). Can edit and revise short descriptions of Fiestas Patrias activities with peers, adding details and suggestions (e.g., 'Let's add more information about the parade, like who will carry the Panamanian flag and what songs the band will play.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h3 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h3>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 57%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 10%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows pictures of different Fiestas Patrias activities (e.g., a band marching, dancers in polleras, a student waving a flag). Students write one word or a short phrase in their notebooks describing the talent or activity they see in each picture (e.g., 'band', 'dance', 'flag').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a simple descriptive sentence on the board about one of the pictures, modeling the target grammar and vocabulary, for example: "The talented students *will play* the drums in the parade. If they *practice* well, they *will perform* an amazing show." The teacher points to 'talented', 'play', 'drums', 'parade', 'practice', 'perform', 'show', highlighting the future simple and first conditional structure. The teacher explicitly states the objective is to write similar sentences about Fiestas Patrias activities.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the plan for the students in the parade? (Expected answer: 'They will play the drums.')"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What happens if they practice well? (Expected answer: 'They will perform an amazing show.')"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "The Talents Around Us."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short descriptive text (e.g., a school newsletter announcement) about the upcoming Fiestas Patrias celebrations and student performances.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><i>Example text:</i><br>
                "<b>Our Fiestas Patrias Celebration!</b><br>
                This year, our school will celebrate Panama's National Holidays with many talented students! First, the honor roll student *will carry* the Panamanian flag. Then, our school band *will march* and *play* patriotic songs. Sofia *can play* the flute beautifully, so she *will perform* a special song. If the baton twirler *practices* her skill every day, she *will amaze* the audience with her colorful costume. We *will have* a wonderful event! Come and see their amazing performance!"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Compose simple descriptive texts related to Fiestas Patrias celebrations.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the text silently. The teacher asks:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What is the text about? (Gist question: 'Our school's Fiestas Patrias celebration.')</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">True or False: The honor roll student will play the drums. (False)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Who can play the flute? (Sofia)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice writing sentences using the future simple tense for plans, the first conditional for real possibilities, and the modal 'can' to express ability or talent, integrating vocabulary related to Fiestas Patrias events and performances (e.g., 'parade', 'band', 'dance', 'costume', 'practice', 'perform', 'talented', 'excited').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher provides sentences with blanks. Students complete them using the correct form of the verb in parentheses or choosing the appropriate word from a box (future simple, 'can', or first conditional structure).
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I _______ (play) the accordion in the show."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If we _______ (rehearse) a lot, we _______ (be) ready for the performance."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"My friend _______ (sing) very well. She _______ (sing) a traditional song."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice (Guided Sentence Writing):</b> The teacher provides picture prompts or short scenarios about Fiestas Patrias preparations. Students write one to two sentences for each, using the target grammar.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><i>Picture: A student playing a drum.</i> -> "He can play the drums. He will march in the parade."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><i>Scenario: My sister wants to dance in the parade.</i> -> "If my sister practices her dance, she will perform in the parade."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction (Peer Check of Sentences):</b> Students work in pairs. They exchange their completed sentences from the previous activity. They check each other's sentences for correct grammar (future simple, first conditional, 'can') and vocabulary, offering suggestions for improvement. The teacher monitors and provides support, encouraging polite feedback using phrases like, "Can you add more details here?" or "I think this verb needs 'will'."</li>
                </ol>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "The Talents Around Us."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Descriptive Paragraph Writing and Peer Editing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in pairs or small groups (3 students). Each group will imagine they are preparing for a Fiestas Patrias event at their school. They will write a short descriptive paragraph (4-6 sentences) about the event, detailing who will perform, what talents they have, what they will do, and how they will prepare, using the target grammar (future simple, first conditional, 'can') and vocabulary. They must also include at least one cultural expression, such as '¡Viva Panamá!' or mention a 'pollera' costume.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students brainstorm ideas for their Fiestas Patrias performance (e.g., "Our friend Marco can play the drums. Andrea will dance the traditional dance. If she practices with her colorful pollera, she will be amazing!").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group writes their first draft of the descriptive paragraph, focusing on describing plans and abilities for the celebration. They ensure to use words like 'parade', 'band', 'performer', 'costume', 'song', 'dance', 'practice', 'rehearse', 'celebrate', 'talented', 'excited', 'patriotic'.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Groups then exchange their paragraphs with another group for peer editing. They use a simple checklist (provided by the teacher) to review:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are there at least 4 sentences?</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are future simple sentences used correctly?</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are 'if... will' sentences (first conditional) used correctly?</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is 'can' used to express ability?</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are at least 5 target vocabulary words included?</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is the text clear and easy to understand?</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">After receiving feedback, groups revise their paragraphs. The teacher circulates, offering support and clarifying doubts about grammar or vocabulary.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation during collaborative writing and editing, using a checklist for target structures. Peer assessment checklist during revision. Final submission of the revised paragraph.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group submits their final, revised descriptive paragraph about their Fiestas Patrias event preparations and performances.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Grammar (40%):</b> Correct use of future simple, first conditional, and modal 'can' (e.g., 'I will play...', 'If I practice, I will...', 'I can sing...').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary (30%):</b> Appropriate and varied use of Fiestas Patrias vocabulary (e.g., 'parade', 'flag', 'talent', 'costume', 'perform', 'patriotic').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Coherence and Clarity (20%):</b> Paragraph is easy to understand, sentences are logically connected.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration/Editing (10%):</b> Evidence of peer feedback incorporated into the final text.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions individually:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new word or grammar rule you used in your paragraph today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did working with your classmates help you improve your writing?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h4>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing about Fiestas Patrias events did you find easy, and what was challenging?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing you will remember when writing about future plans or abilities in English?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> The collaborative writing and peer editing worked very well, as students were actively engaged in using the target grammar and vocabulary. The structure of the conditional and future simple was still a bit challenging for some, especially in forming complex sentences. For the next lesson, I need to provide more sentence frames or specific examples for students who struggle with sentence construction, and perhaps incorporate a quick review of verb conjugations in the present simple for the 'if' clause of the first conditional. The use of cultural expressions was a nice addition, making the task more authentic.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson focused on producing descriptive written texts. The next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration) will build on this by having students consolidate and summarize information about their Fiestas Patrias plans and performances, potentially preparing a short presentation or summary for the 21st Century Skills Project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>